<title>GREECE: GNN POLL: GREEK MKTS GIVE KARAMANLIS SLIGHT EDGE.</title>
<headline>GNN POLL: GREEK MKTS GIVE KARAMANLIS SLIGHT EDGE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek markets gave Costas</p>
<p>Karamanlis a slight edge over rivals George Souflias and current</p>
<p>president Miltiadis Evert in a tight race for the leadership of</p>
<p>the conservative New Democracy party in an informal Reuters</p>
<p>poll.</p>
<p>New Democracy's party congress is going to be held in March</p>
<p>21-23.</p>
<p>Thirty-three bankers, brokers and fund managers participated</p>
<p>in the poll that was conducted on March 12 and March 13.</p>
<p>Results:</p>
<p>1) Who do you think is going to be elected president of the</p>
<p>conservative New Democracy opposition party?</p>
<p>    Karamanlis    11 votes  or 33.33%</p>
<p>    Souflias	10 votes  or 30.30%</p>
<p>    Evert	    9 votes  or 27.27%</p>
<p>    Polydoras	0	  or     0%</p>
<p>    None/no answer 3	  or  9.09%</p>
<p>2) Whom would you like to see president of the New Democracy</p>
<p>party?</p>
<p>    Karamanlis    15 votes  or 45.45%</p>
<p>    Souflias	10 votes  or 30.30%</p>
<p>    Evert	    0 votes  or  0%</p>
<p>    Polydoras	1 vote   or  3.03%</p>
<p>    None	     7 votes  or 21.21%</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
